          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"uncertainty-decomposition-aleatoric-vs-epistemic\">Uncertainty Decomposition: Aleatoric vs. Epistemic</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Not all uncertainty is equal. This notebook decomposes prediction uncertainty into:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Aleatoric uncertainty</strong> \u2014 irreducible noise in the data (e.g., measurement error)</li>\n<li><strong>Epistemic uncertainty</strong> \u2014 reducible uncertainty from limited data or model capacity</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We use the <code>EnsembleDecomposition</code> class with bootstrap refitting to quantify each component\non the <strong>synthetic heteroscedastic</strong> dataset (where noise varies with input features).</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
